:: background-launch.bat.example — launch child processes from a .bat with no window.
::
:: HOW TO USE:
::   1. Copy this file, rename it to  my-launch.bat
::   2. Replace the placeholder paths and commands below.
::   3. If this runs at login, DO NOT put the .bat in the startup folder —
::      wrap it with startup.vbs.example instead (see that file).
::
:: Rule: never use  start /min  (it leaves a minimized window on the taskbar).
:: Use PowerShell Start-Process -WindowStyle Hidden so the child gets no window at all.

@echo off
cd /d "C:\path\to\your\project"

:: --- launch a Node server in the background (no window) ---
powershell -WindowStyle Hidden -NoProfile -Command "Start-Process 'node' -ArgumentList 'server.js' -WindowStyle Hidden"

:: --- launch a tunnel with arguments, in the background (no window) ---
powershell -WindowStyle Hidden -NoProfile -Command "Start-Process 'cloudflared' -ArgumentList 'tunnel','--url','http://localhost:8080' -WindowStyle Hidden"

:: --- launch a Python service with the windowless interpreter ---
pythonw.exe worker.py

:: No  pause  at the end — pause would leave a zombie cmd.exe waiting forever.
